class.description:
[ResourceDatabase] loads resources once and holds strong references to them, so they stay in memory until they are removed, even when no scene uses them any more. Hand it a [PreloadList] with [method preload_from_list], or single paths with [method preload_resource], or store resources you created yourself with [method add_resource].
Loaded resources are stored under their resource path. As long as they are stored, [method ResourceLoader.load] of that path returns the stored instance without reading the disk again. A key that is not a path (for example [code]"hero_sword"[/code]) is only known to the database: [method get_resource] finds it, [method ResourceLoader.load] does not.
[method find_resources] and [method find_keys] find entries by pattern and type. Patterns are case-insensitive; [code]%[/code] matches any run of characters: [code]"items/sword"[/code] (exact), [code]"items/%"[/code] (prefix), [code]"%.tres"[/code] (suffix), [code]"%sword%"[/code] (contains). A pattern matches an entry if it matches its path or one of its keys. The type is a native class or a script [code]class_name[/code]; inherited classes match too.
The lists named in [member ProjectSettings.filesystem/resources/preload_lists] are preloaded at startup, before the autoloads (not in the editor).
Every stored resource stays in memory until [method remove_matching] or [method clear]. Preload small or frequently used resources; [method get_memory_usage] gives an estimate. All methods can be called from any thread; [signal preload_finished] is emitted on the main thread.
[b]Note:[/b] [constant ResourceLoader.CACHE_MODE_REPLACE] updates a stored resource in place. [constant ResourceLoader.CACHE_MODE_IGNORE] returns a new instance and leaves the database unchanged.
[b]Note:[/b] Without thread support (the default Web export) or on a single-core device, [method preload_from_list] always loads synchronously.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var list := PreloadList.new()
list.paths = PackedStringArray(["res://items/sword.tres", "res://items/shield.tres"])
list.keys = { "hero_sword": "res://items/sword.tres" }
ResourceDatabase.preload_finished.connect(func(_list, error): print("Preloaded: ", error_string(error)))
ResourceDatabase.preload_from_list(list)

# Later, anywhere:
var sword: Item = ResourceDatabase.get_resource("hero_sword")
var swords := ResourceDatabase.find_resources("%sword%", "Item")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var list = new PreloadList();
list.Paths = ["res://items/sword.tres", "res://items/shield.tres"];
list.Keys = new Godot.Collections.Dictionary<string, string> { { "hero_sword", "res://items/sword.tres" } };
ResourceDatabase.Singleton.PreloadFinished += (preloadList, error) => GD.Print("Preloaded: ", error);
ResourceDatabase.PreloadFromList(list);

// Later, anywhere:
var sword = ResourceDatabase.GetResource("hero_sword");
var swords = ResourceDatabase.FindResources("%sword%", "Item");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
